# Environments
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template
# The production template MUST travel with the clone. `.env.*` above would
# otherwise swallow it, and a deployment warning that lives only in a
# gitignored file is a warning that never reaches the next machine — which is
# exactly how the INTEGRATION_ENCRYPTION_KEY trap fired twice already.
!.env.prod.example

# --- Deployment runtime state (infra/docker-compose.prod.yml) ---------------
# Let's Encrypt account keys and certificate PRIVATE KEYS live here. Never
# commit this directory.
infra/certbot/conf/
infra/certbot/www/
# Generated on the server from infra/nginx/orkest.conf.template by DEPLOY.md
# step 3; carries the deployment's own hostname, so it is per-host, not shared.
infra/nginx/conf.d/*.conf

# MCP server config — holds a live 21st.dev API_KEY inline.
# To share this with the team instead, replace the literal key with "${MAGIC_API_KEY}"
# (Claude Code expands env vars in .mcp.json), keep the real value in .env, and
# un-ignore this file.
.mcp.json

